From: Prarit Bhargava <prarit@redhat.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 10:45:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bump github.com/klauspost/compress to v1.20.2 for
 CVE-2026-116591

go-vendor-tools.toml's [archive] pre_commands bumps
github.com/klauspost/compress to v1.20.2 before the vendor archive is
generated, but that only ever runs against the vendor checkout, never
against the plain source tarball (Source0). Mirror the same go.mod/go.sum
result into the %prep source tree so go build -mod=vendor does not reject
the build as inconsistent vendoring.

Computed via a real go get github.com/klauspost/compress@v1.20.2 against
the prometheus v3.13.5 source after Patch5 (go-openapi/swag bump), then
go mod tidy (not hand-edited). Tidying also drops stale go.sum entries
for the superseded go-openapi/swag v0.26.0 lines left by Patch5.

Upstream: https://github.com/klauspost/compress/commit/7f5d8528720c895a6106f201719f87eb030a565d

CVE-2026-116591: klauspost/compress zstd decoder can panic on crafted
two-block frames prior to 1.20.2.

HUM-11181
HUM-11254
